<title>UK: Kingfisher extends gains on talk of upgrades.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher extends gains on talk of upgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kingfisher Plc extended their gains on Wednesday, coming within a few pence of their record peak set last week, amid talk analysts are raising their earnings forecasts.</p>
<p>Upgrades and talk of more upgrades came as the UK retailer posted a 36 percent jump in pre-tax pre-exceptional profits to 390.2 million stg in the year ended February 1.</p>
<p>At 1020 GMT, the shares were up 19-1/2p to 694,having risen as high as 697, just 3p from their all-time high.</p>
</text>
